---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
---

<GuideLayout 
  title="Private Label vs. Custom Manufacturing: Choosing Your Path"
  type="BUSINESS STRATEGY"
  description="Navigate the choice between Private Label and OEM/Custom manufacturing to optimize your brand's growth and margins."
>
  <p>When you launch or scale an activewear brand, you'll encounter two primary manufacturing models: <strong>Private Label</strong> and <strong>Custom Manufacturing</strong>. Choosing the right one is critical for your capital and market timing.</p>
  
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-12">
    <div class="p-8 bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100">
      <h4 class="text-[#8E6E8E] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-4">1. Private Label</h4>
      <p class="text-sm">Adding your branding to our proven, high-performance patterns. Low MOQ (50 pcs) and fast lead times (7-15 days).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-8 bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl">
      <h4 class="text-[#C9A84C] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-4">2. Custom Manufacturing</h4>
      <p class="text-sm">Full OEM development from tech packs. Unique measurements and exclusive fabrics. Higher MOQ (300+ pcs) and 45-60 day lead times.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Which Model is Right for You?</h3>
  <p>Most successful brands follow a hybrid approach. Start with Private Label for core essentials to build cash flow, while developing "hero" pieces through Full Custom manufacturing to establish your unique brand identity.</p>

  <div class="mt-12 p-8 bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200">
    <h3 class="mt-0">Free Brand Consultation</h3>
    <p>Not sure where to start? Our consultants can review your vision and recommend the most cost-effective path for your specific business stage.</p>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
